@startuml
!theme vibrant
title Data Loading Flowchart

start

:**Initialization & Setup** \n Generates list of all possible time samples;
note right
    This generates a master list of all samples.
    Each sample contains a unique bin name (e.g., 'bin_123')
    and its corresponding weekly data prefix, which is used
    to easily locate the correct Zarr file on disk.
end note

while (For each batch \n requests a batch of indices) is (true)

    while (For each index in batch) is (true)

        :__getitem__ (index);
        :Get time bin & week string for the index;
                :Call TwoWeekZarrLoader.get_data_for_bin();
        note right
            **TwoWeekZarrLoader**
            Lazily loads and caches weekly data from Zarr stores.
            This avoids re-reading and re-processing the same
            data files repeatedly, improving efficiency.
        end note
        if (Is week's data in cache?) then (no)
            :Load and process all Zarr files for that week;

        endif
        :Get specific bin data from cache;

        :Add node features & targets to HeteroData;

        :Return single HeteroData graph;

    endwhile


        :DataLoader collects all HeteroData objects for the batch;

endwhile


:Yield Batched Graph to Model;

stop
@enduml